# Breezy Does It (levels/solo/breezy.txt), the fired-up route: the fast, risky one. The same
# start; at the fork take the low lane through its quick nugget line (fired up is the counter
# filled last), call the band (Down) as the line ends, hop the fan pit, and jump the canal's
# long gaps with the fired-up stride (jump, toot as he starts to fall): the crumbling island
# (off it before it drops), the headwind gap (toot early, above the wind), the last island
# under a ceiling vent (jump from its clear end). Over the bank's hole; at the nerve fork the
# climb (land on the crumbling ledge by letting go of Right, jump and toot onto the spiky
# roof, hop along it), then the shout chorus to the plunger: toot off the fans, let go of
# Right to land on the climb's crumbling stones. Fired up the whole way.
